      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF, the seller is typically responsible for providing the necessary shipping documents, including the Bill of Lading, commercial invoice, and any relevant customs documents. The Bill of Lading is a key document that shows proof of ownership and details of the shipment, while the commercial invoice itemizes the goods and provides a detailed description of their value. You can usually verify with your freight forwarder or shipper to confirm the specific documents required for your shipment.",
      "source": "target",
